.TH DOCKER-PRUNE-DAEMON 8 "October 2026" "docker-prune-daemon 1.0.0" "System Administration Utilities"
.SH NAME
docker-prune-daemon \- lightweight autonomous disk space reclaim daemon for Docker environments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B docker-prune-daemon
.RB [ \-interval
.IR duration ]
.RB [ \-threshold
.IR percent ]
.RB [ \-until
.IR duration ]
.RB [ \-dry-run ]
.RB [ \-once ]
.RB [ \-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B docker-prune-daemon
is a zero-dependency background daemon engineered in Go that monitors filesystem utilization via atomic
.BR statfs (2)
syscalls and reclaims unused Docker containers, dangling images, and build caches when disk pressure reaches a configurable watermark.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-interval " duration"
Polling interval between disk audits (default:
.BR 30m ).
.TP
.BI \-threshold " percent"
Disk usage percentage watermark (1\-99) required to trigger a prune cycle (default:
.BR 80 ).
.TP
.BI \-until " duration"
Only prune Docker resources created before the specified duration (default:
.BR 24h ).
.TP
.B \-dry-run
Inspect filesystem watermarks and log intended actions without executing destructive Docker prune commands.
.TP
.B \-once
Execute a single audit cycle and exit deterministically.
.TP
.B \-version
Print version string and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DOCKER_DATA_ROOT
Target filesystem path inspected via
.BR statfs (2)
(default:
.BR / ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean shutdown via signal handler or successful single-pass execution.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration validation failure or unrecoverable initialization error.
